{
  "id": "s04-l01",
  "unit": "s04-conjuncts",
  "title": "Conjuncts 1: see-through stacks",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**Sometimes two consonants have no vowel between them.** Bengali then joins them into one block, a **conjunct (যুক্তবর্ণ juktoborno)**. The invisible glue is **্ (hoshonto)**, which removes the inherent `o`: ক is `ko`, ক্ is just `k`.\n\nToday's conjuncts are 'see-through': you can still spot both letters. **ন্ত** (n+t), **স্ত** (s+t: রাস্তা `rasta`), **ন্দ** (n+d: মন্দির `mondir`), **ন্ধ** (n+dh: বন্ধু `bondhu`), **স্ক** (s+k: স্কুল `skul`, নমস্কার `nomoshkar`).\n\n**Read the first part, then the second.** The first letter is usually squeezed or on the left; the second sits below or to the right.\n\n**After a final conjunct the `o` usually comes back**: শান্ত is `shanto`, not *shant*.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "cj-hoshonto",
      "bn": "ক্",
      "tr": "k",
      "en": "্ (hoshonto): kills the inherent vowel, so ক্ = just 'k'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ্ (U+09CD), name hoshonto (হসন্ত). Usually invisible: it is what joins letters into conjuncts. Shown on ক."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-nto",
      "bn": "ন্ত",
      "tr": "nto",
      "en": "n + t (ন + ত)",
      "notes": "ন U+09A8 + ্ U+09CD + ত U+09A4. Very common: পর্যন্ত, শান্ত."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-sto",
      "bn": "স্ত",
      "tr": "sto",
      "en": "s + t (স + ত); স says 's' here",
      "notes": "স U+09B8 + ্ + ত U+09A4. রাস্তা rasta; but নাস্তা is usually said nashta."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-ndo",
      "bn": "ন্দ",
      "tr": "ndo",
      "en": "n + d (ন + দ)",
      "notes": "ন + ্ + দ U+09A6. মন্দির mondir."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-ndho",
      "bn": "ন্ধ",
      "tr": "ndho",
      "en": "n + dh (ন + ধ)",
      "notes": "ন + ্ + ধ U+09A7. বন্ধু bondhu, সন্ধ্যা shondha."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-sko",
      "bn": "স্ক",
      "tr": "sko",
      "en": "s/sh + k (স + ক)",
      "notes": "স + ্ + ক U+0995. স্কুল skul; নমস্কার nomoshkar (said with sh)."
    },
    {
      "id": "shanto",
      "bn": "শান্ত",
      "tr": "shanto",
      "en": "calm / quiet",
      "notes": "Also a common boy's name."
    }
  ],
